The whole story in one line

1943 Neural Networks → 1956 Symbolic AI → 1980s Expert Systems → 1990s Machine Learning → 2012 Deep Learning → 2017 Transformers → 2022 Generative AI → 2024 Reasoning → 2026 AI Agents

The three biggest turning points

1956 — AI is born as a field
Humans begin deliberately trying to build machine intelligence.

2012 — Deep learning changes the game
Machines begin learning representations from enormous datasets rather than relying primarily on human-engineered rules.

2017–2026 — Transformers → LLMs → Agents
AI moves from recognizing and predicting to generating, reasoning, using tools, and taking actions.

The trajectory is remarkably clear:

Rules → Learning → Deep Learning → Generation → Reasoning → Agency

That final step—from an AI that answers to an AI that acts—is arguably the defining transition of the current era.
